cons.handler: do not use SAVERDIR when the build did not define it

Building for a uClinux target stops here:

  cons.handler.c:221:55: error: 'SAVERDIR' undeclared (first use in this function)

configure decides whether to build the console saver by matching the host
triplet against linux*:

  cons_saver=""
  case $host_os in
  linux*)
      cons_saver=yes
  esac

and src/Makefile.am defines SAVERDIR only `if CONS_SAVER`. On a uClinux
toolchain the triplet is arm-buildroot-uclinuxfdpiceabi, so $host_os is
"uclinuxfdpiceabi" and does not match -- while cons.handler.c decides the same
question with #ifdef __linux__, which the compiler does define, because this is
Linux. Two notions of "is this Linux" that agree on every ordinary target and
disagree here.

Rather than argue with either, make the reference conditional on the macro that
actually says whether the saver exists. Without it the code falls through to the
path already there for "console is not a tty or execl() failed", which sets
console_flag to 0 and carries on -- the same thing that happens on any machine
whose console is not a Linux virtual terminal, which includes this one.

Upstream status: not submitted, though the mismatch is upstream's and would be
worth reporting.

--- a/src/cons.handler.c
+++ b/src/cons.handler.c
@@ -185,12 +185,16 @@
         else
         {
             /* Child */
+#ifdef SAVERDIR
             char *tty_name;
+#endif
 
             /* Close the extra pipe ends */
             status = close (pipefd1[1]);
             status = close (pipefd2[0]);
+#ifdef SAVERDIR
             tty_name = ttyname (0);
+#endif
             /* Bind the pipe 0 to the standard input */
             do
             {
@@ -213,6 +217,7 @@
                 if (!ok)
                     break;
 
+#ifdef SAVERDIR
                 if (tty_name != NULL)
                 {
                     char *mc_conssaver;
@@ -221,6 +226,7 @@
                     mc_conssaver = mc_build_filename (SAVERDIR, "cons.saver", (char *) NULL);
                     execl (mc_conssaver, "cons.saver", tty_name, (char *) NULL);
                 }
+#endif /* SAVERDIR */
                 /* Console is not a tty or execl() failed */
             }
             while (0);
